<% content_for :title, "Refunds" %>

<div class="rise">
  <div class="mb-8 flex flex-col gap-4 sm:flex-row sm:items-center sm:justify-between">
    <div>
      <h1 class="desk-title text-3xl text-ink">refunds</h1>
      <p class="mt-2 max-w-lg text-sm text-ink-dim">
        Every refund runs <span class="font-mono text-xs text-ink">requested → processing → settled</span>.
        Money books only when Stripe's signed webhook confirms it.
      </p>
    </div>
    <%= link_to "issue refund", new_refund_path, class: "btn btn-primary self-start sm:self-auto" %>
  </div>

  <% if demo_mode? %>
    <div class="panel mb-8 p-6">
      <p class="meta mb-2">start here</p>
      <p class="mb-5 max-w-2xl text-sm text-ink-dim">
        A double-entry ledger for refunds and payouts. Money books only when Stripe's
        signed webhook confirms it, never on request. Balances are summed from an
        append-only log, so nothing can drift. Run the whole loop in about a minute:
      </p>
      <ol class="space-y-2.5 text-sm text-ink">
        <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="font-mono text-xs text-credit">1</span><span><%= link_to "Issue a refund", new_refund_path, class: "text-ink underline decoration-line underline-offset-4 hover:text-credit" %> on any charge. It lands in <span class="font-mono text-xs text-pending">processing</span>, waiting on Stripe.</span></li>
        <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="font-mono text-xs text-credit">2</span><span>Open that refund and <span class="text-ink">play Stripe's webhook → settles</span>. That is the only thing that moves money.</span></li>
        <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="font-mono text-xs text-credit">3</span><span>Watch the reversal land on the <%= link_to "ledger", ledger_path, class: "text-ink underline decoration-line underline-offset-4 hover:text-credit" %>, colored by sign.</span></li>
        <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="font-mono text-xs text-credit">4</span><span>Open <%= link_to "reconciliation", reconciliation_path, class: "text-ink underline decoration-line underline-offset-4 hover:text-credit" %>: it proves every entry balances and the book sums to zero (and matches Stripe to the halala once real keys are wired).</span></li>
        <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="font-mono text-xs text-credit">5</span><span>Back on the settled refund, <span class="text-ink">replay the webhook</span>. The ledger stays booked exactly once.</span></li>
      </ol>
      <p class="mt-5 font-mono text-xs text-ink-faint">
        demo mode · production runs with it off, where only a signature-verified webhook settles and these shortcuts never exist
      </p>
    </div>
  <% end %>

  <div class="panel overflow-x-auto">
    <table class="ledger-table">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>refund</th>
          <th>charge</th>
          <th class="text-right">amount</th>
          <th>status</th>
          <th class="text-right">created</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <% @refunds.each do |refund| %>
          <tr>
            <td><%= link_to "##{refund.id}", refund, class: "font-mono text-sm text-ink hover:text-credit" %></td>
            <td><%= link_to refund.charge.stripe_payment_intent_id, refund.charge, class: "font-mono text-xs text-ink-dim hover:text-ink" %></td>
            <td class="text-right"><%= amount(refund.amount_cents) %></td>
            <td><%= status_badge(refund.status) %></td>
            <td class="text-right font-mono text-xs text-ink-faint"><%= refund.created_at.strftime("%b %-d · %H:%M") %></td>
          </tr>
        <% end %>
        <% if @refunds.empty? %>
          <tr><td colspan="5" class="px-4 py-16 text-center font-mono text-sm text-ink-faint">no refunds issued yet</td></tr>
        <% end %>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
</div>
